FULL TERMS (ENGLISH)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Definitions

   "Program" means the webwarden and datz software distributed from this
   repository, in source or packaged form, together with modifications and
   derived builds of it.

   "License Manager" means the `licensing` module shipped with the Program. It
   stores a first-run timestamp in ~/.datz/state.json, verifies a signed license
   string, and decides whether a run is licensed (Pro) or on a free trial.

   "Trial" means the free 20-day evaluation period that begins the first time
   the Program is executed for real on a machine.

   "License Key" means a signed string of the form DATZ1.<payload>.<signature>
   minted by the Licensor with the private half of the Ed25519 key pair whose
   public half is embedded in the Program.

   "Licensor" means Ahmad Roziqin, the copyright holder.

   "You" means the individual or entity running the Program.

2. Source availability, not free commercial use

   You may read, study, audit, print, and share unmodified copies of the source
   for evaluation, teaching, and security research. You may open pull requests.
   Public source code does not grant a free commercial licence; running the
   Program beyond the Trial requires a License Key (section 4).

3. Grant during the Trial

   For the length of the Trial you may run the Program on your own machine, for
   authorized assessments (section 9), at no cost, without redistribution rights.
   The Trial is machine-global, not per-product: the Program records when it was
   first seen and will not silently renew the period by reinstalling, renaming
   the state file, or moving the binary.

4. Commercial licence

   4.1  One License Key is issued for one named customer and one product scope.
        A key may be scoped to a single product (webwarden, netwarden) or to all
        products of the Licensor.
   4.2  A License Key may be active on the machines of one customer acting as
        one team. Selling, lending, sub-licensing, publishing, or otherwise
        redistributing a License Key is not permitted.
   4.3  A License Key may carry an expiry date and an optional host limit. The
        Program enforces both.
   4.4  Licences are sold as time-limited memberships: 30, 90, or 365 days from
        the date the key is minted. The expiry date travels inside the key and
        the Program enforces it. The terms shown at the point of purchase
        prevail.
   4.5  Ordering and enquiry: https://lisensi.ziqintzy.my.id/

5. Licence enforcement

   5.1  The Program checks the licence before running any work command and prints
        the resulting tier in its banner, in the terminal, and in every report
        artifact (Markdown, HTML, JSON).
   5.2  Commands that only read state or remove rules the Program previously
        added are deliberately left free, so that an expired trial can never
        strand live traffic behind orphaned rules.
   5.3  You agree not to circumvent, disable, reverse-engineer around, patch,
        fork with the purpose of removing, or otherwise defeat the License
        Manager, and not to distribute a build in which it has been defeated.
   5.4  You agree not to strip, forge, or alter the licence watermark, banner, or
        report stamp.
   5.5  Honest disclosure: the Program is written in Python and its source is
        public, so a determined user can bypass the gate. Section 5.3 is a
        contractual boundary, not a technical guarantee. Buying a licence is how
        you support continued development of the tool.

6. Key issuance

   Only the Licensor holds the private signing key. The Program can verify a
   License Key but cannot mint one. Any tool claiming to generate working keys
   for this Program is unaffiliated, is likely fraudulent, and voids no term of
   this licence.

7. Copyleft-free contributions

   Contributions you send to this repository may be adopted, licensed, and sold
   by the Licensor. Contributing means you grant that permission and confirm you
   have the right to give it.

8. Trademarks

   The names webwarden, netwarden, datz, and the associated marks stay with the
   Licensor. They do not transfer with the source.

9. Authorized use only

   9.1  You may point the Program only at hosts, networks, accounts, and
        applications that you own or that you have written permission to test
        (a bug-bounty programme scope, an employer's own estate, a training lab,
        or a customer engagement).
   9.2  The Program requires explicit confirmation flags for that reason, keeps
        its checks read-only by design, and refuses out-of-scope targets.
   9.3  You are solely responsible for complying with the law of your
        jurisdiction and with the rules of the programme you are testing under.
        The Licensor accepts no liability for misuse.

10. Warranty disclaimer

   THE PROGRAM IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. IT FINDS WHAT IT FINDS
   AND MAY MISLABEL IT. EVERY RESULT MUST BE VERIFIED BY A HUMAN BEFORE IT IS
